hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"91","[AI-translation] Rabi bin Sabrah Juhani se, apne walid (Raziyallahu anhuma) se riwayat hai: Ke Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ne mutah nikah se mana farmaya, aur farmaya: 'Khabardar, beshak wo tumhare is din se lekar qayamat ke din tak haram hai. Aur jo kuch de chuka use wapas na le.'"
"92","[AI-translation] Hazrat Anas bin Malik (Raziyallahu anhu) se riwayat hai, unhon ne kaha: Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ne farmaya: 'Beshak har deen ka ek khulq [numayan wasf] hai. Aur beshak Islam ka khulq haya hai.' [Muhammad ne kaha: Ibrahim bin Abdul Aziz ne mujhe bayan kiya, Ali bin Zuhair ne hamen bayan kiya, Ali bin Ayyash ne hamen bayan kiya, Abbad bin Kaseer se, Umar bin Abdul Aziz (Rahimahullah) se, Zuhri se, Anas bin Malik se, unhon ne kaha: Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ne farmaya:] 'Beshak har deen ka ek khulq [numayan wasf] hai. Aur beshak Islam ka khulq haya hai.' [Ye hadees apni sanad mein dohrai gayi hai]."
"93","[AI-translation] Rabi bin Sabrah Juhani se riwayat hai: Ke un ke walid ne kaha: Main ne Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ke zamane mein Bani Amir ki ek aurat se do surkh chadaron [ke meher] par mutah kiya, 'aur Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ne hamen mutah [nikah] se mana farmaya.' [Rawi ne] kaha: Aur main ne Rabi bin Sabrah ko Umar bin Abdul Aziz (Rahimahullah) ko ye bayan karte hue suna jabke main baitha hua tha."
